# Normalize line endings: LF in the repository and in every checkout.
#
# ``core.autocrlf`` is machine-wide on some Windows setups, which writes CRLF
# into the working tree while the index stores LF. That makes ``git status``
# report untouched files as modified and fails ``ruff format --check``
# (``[tool.ruff.format] line-ending = "lf"``) on an otherwise clean checkout.
# Per-file attributes take precedence over ``core.autocrlf``, so pinning
# ``eol=lf`` here fixes both without asking contributors to change their Git
# configuration.
* text=auto eol=lf
